# Workspace Recipe LLM Guide

## Purpose

Inspect, validate, preview, and render recipes.

## When To Run

- Before creating files.
- Before hand-writing shaped files.
- When validating recipes.
- Between `enclosure workspace rules` and `enclosure health`.

## How To Read The Result

- Listing shows available recipes.
- Summary shows inputs and targets.
- Check validates metadata and rendering.
- Dry run shows create/skip status.
- Shell preview shows rendered content.
- Recipes may compose `fragment` recipes.

## Examples

- First run: `enclosure workspace recipe --list`, `enclosure workspace recipe <name> --show`, then `enclosure workspace recipe <name> <path> --shell`.
- Inspect recipes before creating files.
- Keep ownership in `workspace.recipe.roles_map`.
- Provide required inputs as variables.
- If dry run skips a target, preserve or edit manually.
- If check fails, fix the recipe before generation.

## Agent Tips

- Prefer local recipes over inventing scaffolding.
- Inspect a recipe before rendering it.
- Use `--shell` as the convention oracle.
- Run `enclosure workspace recipe --check` or dry run before writing.
